# Dual geometry for G.2.5

The actual natural coordinates construct the three annihilator points, their
direct decomposition and the contragredient natural marking. Full point
stabilizers in LT normalize the corresponding U-conjugates. Their root lifts
satisfy the printed displacement and fixation bounds on the literal lower
quotient, using its canonical coordinates.

The six actual frame roots prove full I-invariance of S₃. The plane-stabilizer
factorization makes the dual orbit map well-defined, and concrete flag
transitivity propagates the root calculation to every incident flag. The
resulting map on the literal lower quotient satisfies every field of
Projective.Criterion, with all three pair-intersection marks.

The concrete dual fixed-space and conjugate-radical bridges also identify
all three marked images under any actual homogeneous dual equivalence,
including their ordinary coordinates and orders. Multiplicity zero is
retained. Earlier structural premises remain with their source producers;
the universal G.1.3 recognition implication and its application remain with
the recognition assembly owner.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
G.1.1–4 and G.2.5, printed pp.327–328,335–336.
